content:
**Rule.** The child additions in the opening past-due release of a Disability Compensation award are:

- one child addition for each recorded minor child plus one school-child addition for each recorded school child, when the award records both;
- one child addition for each recorded minor child, when it records minor children and no school child;
- one school-child addition for each recorded school child, when it records school children and no minor child;
- nothing, when it records no child.

**Counting and months.** Minor children recorded are the child additions on the award less the child removals; school children recorded are the school-child additions less the school-child removals. Each minor child's addition is counted for the whole months elapsed from the most recent child addition's effective date to the issue date of the most recent monthly payment, and each school child's addition for the whole months elapsed from the most recent school-child addition's effective date to that same issue date. Of each such run of months, as many as fall in the months owed at the individual unemployability rate — never more than the run itself — take the 100 percent tier's amount (child 146.10, school child 472.95), and the rest take the award's own tier.

**Worked figure (hypothetical award at Disability Compensation (70% Combined Rating); most recent monthly payment issued 1 March 2026; no months owed at the individual unemployability rate).**

- Two minor children; the most recent child addition is effective 12 November 2025: 3 whole months. 102.27 for 3 months for each child: 306.81 multiplied by 2, that is 613.62.
- One school child; the school-child addition is effective 25 August 2025: 6 whole months. 331.07 for 6 months: 1986.42.
- Child additions in the release: 613.62 plus 1986.42, that is 2600.04.
